namespace pdg { /**

\class Image
\brief A bitmap image that can be blitted onto the screen

You can create an image from a file or an offscreen Port, or load it from resource files with the ResourceManager.

\code
    const img = new pdg.Image("myImage.png");
    // Given an offscreen Port named surface:
    const live = new pdg.Image(surface, pdg.SharedSurface);
\endcode

Images are just a data object. Methods in Port are used to draw them onscreen.

\sa Port.drawImage()
\sa ResourceManager.getImage()

\ingroup Graphics



**/ }

/**
\fn pdg::Image::Image(string filename)
\brief Load a bitmap image from a file.
\param filename Image file path, resolved using the runtime's file/resource lookup.
\see Image(Port, boolean), ResourceManager::getImage()
*/
